<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ten Years' War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1868">1868</a>–<a href="/years/1878">1878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ten Years' War of 1868–1878 was the first major Cuban war of independence against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>. It began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carlos-manuel-de-cespedes">Carlos Manuel de Céspedes</a> freed his enslaved workers and proclaimed independence at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/la-demajagua">La Demajagua</a> on 10 October 1868, and was fought by the Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cuba">Cuba</a> in Arms mainly in the east of the island. It ended with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pact-of-zanjon">Pact of Zanjón</a>, without independence or the full abolition of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavery">slavery</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ten-years-war.jpg" alt="Ten Years' War" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ramon Padró i Pedret · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Embarcament_dels_voluntaris_catalans_al_port_de_Barcelona.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
